  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan; Block Plan; Design & Access Statement; Transport Assessment; CEN-CHA-XX-DR-A-0007; CEN-CHA-ZZ-DR-A-0009; CEN-CHA-ZZ-DR-A-0010; CEN-CHA-XX-DR-A-0008; CEN-CHA-ZZ-DR-A-0006.\r\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) and the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015, or any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting those Orders, the development hereby approved shall be used only for purposes falling within Use Class C2 (children's care home), and for no other purpose.\r\rReason: To ensure that the use of the premises remains appropriate to the character of the area and the assessment of the application, and to prevent the introduction of alternative uses that could give rise to unacceptable impacts on amenity, traffic or the local environment without further consideration by the Local Planning Authority.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be occupied by no more than 2 residents and 2 members of staff (excluding ad hoc visiting specialists/ therapists) at any one time.\r\rReason: To minimise the impact of the development on the occupiers of neighbouring properties and to ensure that car parking provision complies with the Council's adopted standards.\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until details of and appropriate layout for the 1 long-stay and 1 short-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the details stated above prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport. \r\r"
  ],
